    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0798" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/1035: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-27T13:00:00+00:00">September 27, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 27—10:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>64. Request information as to accuracy statement in press to the effect that the
                    period during which Spain will enjoy the benefit of tariff reductions made other
                    countries under Trade Agreement Act<anchor n="21" xml:id="d592-f1"/> has been
                    extended to December 31.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d592-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d592-f1" n="21" xml:id="d592-f1-content">
                <p>Approved June 12, 1934; 48 Stat. 943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d592-f2" n="22" xml:id="d592-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 63, September 28, noon, the Department informed the Ambassador
                    that the duties proclaimed in connection with Belgium, Haiti, and Sweden had
                    been extended to Spain until January 1, 1936 (611.4231/1036a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
